# Packages allowed in a Roxora image although they are not in the Ubuntu
# server cloud image reference and do not match a hardware-layer pattern.
# Format: <package> <reason>. All of them come from the Ubuntu archive unless
# the reason says otherwise.

# Roxora's own additions and the board support package
armbian-bsp-cli-radxa-rock-4d-edge  board support package, filtered to its hardware parts (docs/bsp-classification.md); built with the image
armbian-bsp-cli-armsom-cm5-io-edge  board support package, filtered to its hardware parts (docs/bsp-classification.md); built with the image

# Armbian's minimal package list (config/cli/noble/main/packages); plain Ubuntu packages
alsa-utils        Armbian minimal list: audio mixer and ALSA state restore for on-board codecs
debconf-utils     Armbian minimal list: debconf-get-selections and friends
debsums           Armbian minimal list: verify installed package files
dialog            Armbian minimal list: dialog boxes for scripts
fake-hwclock      Armbian minimal list: keeps a sane clock across reboots on boards without a battery-backed RTC
figlet            Armbian minimal list: banner text (no longer used by any motd script)
iw                Armbian minimal list: Wi-Fi configuration; also used by the BSP's Wi-Fi power-save udev rule
libcaca0          dependency of toilet
mmc-utils         Armbian minimal list: eMMC and SD tool (mmc extcsd, boot partitions)
pahole            Armbian minimal list: BTF/DWARF tool used by kernel module builds
toilet            Armbian minimal list: banner text (no longer used by any motd script)
toilet-fonts      dependency of toilet
wireguard-tools   Armbian minimal list: WireGuard userspace tools
wireless-regdb    Armbian minimal list: Wi-Fi regulatory database
wpasupplicant     Armbian minimal list: Wi-Fi client
libpcsclite1      dependency of wpasupplicant
libasound2-data   dependency of alsa-utils
libasound2t64     dependency of alsa-utils
libatopology2t64  dependency of alsa-utils
libfftw3-single3  dependency of alsa-utils
